.TH QUANUXCTL-PREDEPLOY 8 "February 2026" "QuanuX 0.1.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl\-predeploy \- Simulate and validate a NATS capability handshake before payload deployment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl predeploy
.B --payload
.I PATH
.B --target
.I HOSTNAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quanuxctl predeploy
interrogates a target node's Sovereign Habitat. It reads the \fBrequirements.json\fR from the specified payload path, compares it against the \fBcapabilities_registry.yaml\fR central dictionary, and publishes a NATS \fIQUANUX.NODE.HANDSHAKE\fR packet. The target node will respond with an ACK if compatible, or a NACK if the habitat lacks the required capabilities.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-payload \fIPATH\fR
The path to the local payload directory containing the 'requirements.json'.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-target \fIHOSTNAME\fR
The target Habitat node connected to the NATS grid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.EX
quanuxctl predeploy --payload src/payloads/tier4-striker/ --target node-04
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if Handshake ACK (Compatible).
1 if Handshake NACK (Incompatible) or Network/Registry error.
